# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AP-Model-QC artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The evaluation cases. The harness is a dependency, pinned by reference in
# pyproject.toml, and is never vendored here.

# Test-design documents are tracked project output, not scratch work.
!docs/
!docs/testing/
!docs/testing/**

# The code excerpts are DELIBERATELY DEFECTIVE and are tracked. Their .txt
# suffix keeps every formatter and linter away from them; see
# tests/fixtures/excerpts/README.md for why that matters.
!tests/fixtures/
!tests/fixtures/**

# CI-generated test artifacts, regenerated every run.
reports/
allure-results/
allure-report/
junit_*.xml

# Recorded provider responses are tracked, because replay depends on them and
# a fixture changing changes every replay outcome. Nothing here is ignored.

# Provider credentials. Never committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# JetBrains IDE settings. Machine-local and developer-specific: committing
# them makes every teammate editor state a source of merge conflicts. The
# GitHub template ships this line commented out, which reads as present to a
# careless grep and ignores nothing.
.idea/

# Verbatim prompts and working notes. NEVER TRACKED, and the reason is narrow:
# this is the one file a credential could reach by being pasted into a prompt.
# The harness carries the same rule; both repositories need it, because either
# one alone leaves the other able to commit the file.
.claude/logs/
